Cell["Preparation checks executables but does not construct \
generation inputs. Missing FORM skips generation while helper measurements \
remain usable. Nothing installs software. Every prepared run may execute \
once; prepare again for another run.", "Text", ExpressionUUID -> 
          "1911b865-dcf8-49c1-89bb-1cd99c0ce51e"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["4. Measure sequentially", "Section", 
         ExpressionUUID -> "62c8dd0c-fbec-4560-a742-823d0c9415ba"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"report", "=", 
   RowBox[{"BenchmarkRun", "[", "prepared", "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 InitializationCell->False,
 CellLabel->"In[9]:=",ExpressionUUID->"1b857764-8600-4b85-9cb9-ee9587c5db8f"],

Cell["\<\
Each public command runs first: first observation, one warmup, then measured \
repetitions, each with fresh output paths. Its isolated construction, export, \
execution, import, writing/read-back and publication stages follow. \
Multi-file public commands are timed together; staged rows identify each \
library. A progress bar shows completed cases and the current stage. Detailed \
progress is saved in progress.log in the run directory. Logging remains part \
of public-command timing.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"46ef02b6-65dd-497e-8dc3-82a508966bf2"]
}, Open  ]],

